<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Create Polyline (Manual)</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Create Polyline (Manual)</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Create Polyline (Manual)</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command allows you to create a new polyline by manually selecting points on the visible data. As each point is selected using the mouse a straight line is created to the previous point. Every point can be used for creating polyline node – scan data vertices, mesh vertices, point cloud points (including probe points and the points from static stripes), other polyline nodes, datum points, datum lines, and centres of datum spheres and circles. It is not necessary the reference points to be selected. All polylines created by this method will be placed in separate group.&#160;</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">When this command is called the mouse pointer changes to cross.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image021.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">Mouse pointer in</span> <span class="Mode">Create Polyline (Manual)</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Then click with the left mouse button on a visible object or area and the current polyline node will snap to the closest data point. If you click with the right mouse button, the last drawn line will be deleted. Double click to end the polyline. You will exit from this mode and Zoom Window, which is the default mode, will be enabled. This means that if you want to create another polyline, you have to call this command again.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Example</u></span></a></p>
